INDEPENDENT_CLAIM_FREEZE.json was saved before reading imported priority-gate verdicts. The task context already disclosed gate orientations; independence here concerns literal reconstruction, proof checking and controls, not task-context blinding. The complete authentic Kaibel contribution and the complete current TeX were read before the freeze.

Kaibel Problem 1 selects one common undirected spanning tree and sums each separately supplied root cost over its entire induced rooted orientation. Problem 2 selects a fixed directed root and scores destination paths; the manuscript makes no transfer or conclusion about it. The current finite explicit nonnegative integral table is a subclass of the source's real-valued objective under ordinary finite encoding. Transposing every root's arc costs accommodates the opposite rooted-orientation convention.

